<%# Article-history pilot: the wording shown, compared with the wording before it, inside its normal presentation
    (HistoryInlineComparison; the owner, via Sol 2026-11-23 04:31:08Z): the common words once, the added words as
    printed, in the colour of their amendment, and the removed words struck through where they stood. The article's
    number stands on its own line above (laws/_history_article), so the text's own is not shown again
    ([data-history-shown-text]). When no word changed, a line says so: that only Justel's notes differ when the
    archive marks this wording so (notes_only), else, neutrally, that the wording is unchanged (Sol 2026-11-23
    10:08:33Z: a change in the layout alone is no change in the notes).
    Locals: key, old_body, new_body, numac, notes_only. %>
<% comparison, counts = history_inline_comparison(key, old_body, new_body, numac) %>
<% if counts[:added].zero? && counts[:removed].zero? %>
  <p class="not-prose mb-1 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300" data-history-unchanged="<%= local_assigns[:notes_only] ? 'notes' : 'wording' %>"><%= history_label(local_assigns[:notes_only] ? :notes_only : :wording_unchanged).upcase_first %>.</p>
<% end %>
<div data-history-diff data-history-shown-text><%= comparison %></div>
